"Former Iowa State AD calls NIL system 'money laundering'","description":"Former Iowa State athletic director Jamie Pollard delivered a scorching appraisal of college athletics to the Knight Commission, equating NIL as a money-laundering operation.","published":"2026-11-17T19:08:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50512485/former-iowa-state-ad-calls-nil-system-money-laundering","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Purdue rolls with FAA ground stop by taking buses to Iowa","description":"Unable to travel by plane, the Boilermakers rolled with the situation and found some good times on the way.","published":"2026-11-17T11:28:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504665/purdue-faa-ground-stop-bus-iowa","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Heisman of Week 11: Duke's Nate Sheppard has entered the running","description":"In a season in which star running backs seem to be popping up out of nowhere, the Blue Devils' sophomore stands out.","published":"2026-11-17T14:55:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503621/heisman-watch-week-11-duke-nate-sheppard","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on College Football Playoff bubble ahead of committee's third ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-17T15:58:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503628/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-third-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Breaking down the major futures for the Big Ten, from the Heisman to the CFP","description":"Let's evaluate whether a standout performance on a three-loss team and a 10-0 team are real or a mirage in the Big Ten.","published":"2026-11-17T13:02:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50504671/college-football-heisman-trophy-cfp-futures-betting-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Arkansas State tells Butch Jones he's out at end of year","description":"Arkansas State has informed football coach Butch Jones that he's out at the end of the season, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Monday night.","published":"2026-11-17T02:45:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50506952/sources-butch-jones-arkansas-state-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5138451/luke-reynolds","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luke_Reynolds_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":47,"round":2,"team":"DAL","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Luke Reynolds (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luke_Reynolds_(American_football)","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-17T20:10:34Z","intro":"Luke Reynolds is an American college football tight end for the Virginia Tech Hokies. He previously played for the Penn State Nittany Lions.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Reynolds grew up in Westford, Massachusetts and originally attended Lawrence Academy in Groton, Massachusetts. He transferred to Cheshire Academy in Cheshire, Connecticut after his sophomore year. As a senior, he caught 48 passes for 754 yards and nine touchdowns. After the season Reynolds played in the 2024 All-American Bowl.\nReynolds was initially rated a three-star recruit and committed to play college football at Penn State. He was later reranked as a five-star recruit and the best tight end prospect in the 2024 class by 247Sports."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Reynolds joined the Penn State Nittany Lions as an early enrollee in January 2024. He entered his freshman season as a backup at tight end to Tyler Warren. Reynolds finished his first season with the team with nine receptions for 111 yards and one touchdown. He played in all 13 of the Nittany Lions' games as a sophomore and caught 26 passes for 257 yards. After the end of the season, Reynolds entered the NCAA transfer portal.\nReynolds transferred to Virginia Tech, reuniting him with former Penn State head coach James Franklin."}]}}